n onverenigbaar licht op dezelfde geschiedenis. Harry Mulisch bouwt de novelle op als twee delen met een tussenspel, waarin woorden niet eenvoudig vastleggen wat werkelijk gebeurd is. Theater en werkelijkheid raken daardoor met elkaar verstrengeld. Het verhaal vraagt hoe mensen tegenover anderen en zichzelf een overtuigende versie van hun verleden kunnen presenteren.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Gecontroleerde boek- en catalogusbronnen","source_url":"https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_eer001200001_01/_eer001200001_01_0010.php","evidence":[{"type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p188861645"],"reference":"new-work-dossier-readings-038.json#150","checked_at":"2026-11-03T08:04:14.628Z","note":"Mulisch CPNB2000 bound regular Het theater de brief en de waarheid9789074336994, not limitedlinen200copies. Two incompatible funeral narratives; fiction not proof of real accusations."},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","sources":["https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_eer001200001_01/_eer001200001_01_0010.php","https://www.astro.yale.edu/dokkum/mulisch/beschrijving.htm","https://openlibrary.org/works/OL659053W","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p188861645"],"review":"content-amendment-015.json"},{"type":"explicit_contributor_roles","credits":[],"limitation":"Existing schema has one primary Work author; no synthetic combined-author identity or author merge."},{"type":"cover_front_review","cover_id":6460568,"sha256":"793a6c5fc388ba7936f5db35db5d0c671228f1a85df1f3c4c745e72599ae48a9","reference":"cover-semantic-review-014.json","limitation":"Front title/author and source-edition binding; no barcode or exact printing-year claim."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-11-03T08:04:14.628Z","review_batch":"nl-scale-20261102-038"}},{"ref":"m5","relation":"catalog_edition_metadata","key":{"edition_id":"@e5"},"before":null,"after":{"edition_id":"@e5","work_id":"@w5","bound_author_id":636,"bound_title":"Het theater, de brief en de waarheid","bound_language":"dut","bound_isbn13":"9789074336994","format":"hardcover","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6460568-L.jpg?default=false","card_cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6460568-M.jpg?default=false","evidence_url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p188861645","evidence":[{"type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p188861645"],"reference":"new-work-dossier-readings-038.json#150","checked_at":"2026-11-03T08:04:14.628Z","note":"Mulisch CPNB2000 bound regular Het theater de brief en de waarheid9789074336994, not limitedlinen200copies. Two incompatible funeral narratives; fiction not proof of real accusations."},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","sources":["https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_eer001200001_01/_eer001200001_01_0010.php","https://www.astro.yale.edu/dokkum/mulisch/beschrijving.htm","https://openlibrary.org/works/OL659053W","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p188861645"],"review":"content-amendment-015.json"},{"type":"explicit_contributor_roles","credits":[],"limitation":"Existing schema has one primary Work author; no synthetic combined-author identity or author merge."},{"type":"cover_front_review","cover_id":6460568,"sha256":"793a6c5fc388ba7936f5db35db5d0c671228f1a85df1f3c4c745e72599ae48a9","reference":"cover-semantic-review-014.json","limitation":"Front title/author and source-edition binding; no barcode or exact printing-year claim."}],"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-11-03T08:04:14.628Z","review_batch":"nl-scale-20261102-038"}},{"ref":"w6","relation":"works","key":{"native_identity_key":"nlscale:20261102:ol:OL699573W"},"before":null,"after":{"title":"De stille vriend","author_id":638,"first_publish_year":1984,"open_library_id":"OL699573W","cover_id":6754870,"source_type":"open_library","work_type":"novel","native_identity_key":"nlscale:20261102:ol:OL699573W"}},{"ref":"e6","relation":"editions","key":{"open_library_edition_id":"OL2993566M"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":"@w6","open_library_edition_id":"OL2993566M","isbn_13":"9789010053220","isbn_10":null,"title":"De stille vriend","language":"dut","publisher":"Manteau"}},{"ref":"d6","relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","key":{"work_id":"@w6","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":"@w6","language":"nl","bound_author_id":638,"text":"Wanneer George Speerman in Amsterdam een jonge man ziet die hem bekend voorkomt, komt een eerdere ontmoeting opnieuw tot leven. Zijn herinneringen voeren terug naar de jaren zestig en naar Marcel, voor wie hij sterke gevoelens koesterde. Vanuit het latere heden probeert hij die gebeurtenissen te begrijpen. De roman beweegt tussen herinnering en een nieuwe reis naar Frankrijk. Gerard Reve vertelt over verlangen en verbondenheid, terwijl wat George beleeft voortdurend wordt gekleurd door zijn verbeelding en zijn terugblik op vroeger.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Gecontroleerde boek- en catalogusbronnen","source_url":"https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_rev004198601_01/_rev004198601_01_0012.php","evidence":[{"type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p842223533"],"reference":"new-work-dossier-readings-038.json#151","checked_at":"2026-11-03T08:04:14.628Z","note":"GerardReve and GerardKornelisVanHetReve same independently bound author; De stille vriend1984, GeorgeSpeerman fiction not factual autobiography. Exact Manteaupaperback9789010053220."},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","sources":["https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_rev004198601_01/_rev004198601_01_0012.php","https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_rev004198601_01/_rev004198601_01_0002.php","https://openlibrary.org/works/OL699573W","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p842223533"],"review":"content-amendment-015.json"},{"type":"explicit_contributor_roles","credits":[],"limitation":"Existing schema has one primary Work author; no synthetic combined-author identity or author merge."},{"type":"cover_front_review","cover_id":6754870,"sha256":"56e208245e559627bbd15a07f9306eea76005a8045b381b3cb66311b7b0d0e8b","reference":"cover-semantic-review-014.json","limitation":"Front title/author and source-edition binding; no barcode or exact printing-year claim."}],"provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-11-03T08:04:14.628Z","review_batch":"nl-scale-20261102-038"}},{"ref":"m6","relation":"catalog_edition_metadata","key":{"edition_id":"@e6"},"before":null,"after":{"edition_id":"@e6","work_id":"@w6","bound_author_id":638,"bound_title":"De stille vriend","bound_language":"dut","bound_isbn13":"9789010053220","format":"paperback","cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6754870-L.jpg?default=false","card_cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/6754870-M.jpg?default=false","evidence_url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p842223533","evidence":[{"type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p842223533"],"reference":"new-work-dossier-readings-038.json#151","checked_at":"2026-11-03T08:04:14.628Z","note":"GerardReve and GerardKornelisVanHetReve same independently bound author; De stille vriend1984, GeorgeSpeerman fiction not factual autobiography. Exact Manteaupaperback9789010053220."},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","sources":["https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_rev004198601_01/_rev004198601_01_0012.php","https://www.dbnl.org/tekst/_rev004198601_01/_rev004198601_01_0002.php","https://openlibrary.org/works/OL699573W","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p842223533"],"review":"content-amendment-015.json"},{"type":"explicit_contributor_roles","credits":[],"limitation":"Existing schema has one primary Work author; no synthetic combined-author identity or author merge."},{"type":"cover_front_review","cover_id":6754870,"sha256":"56e208245e559627bbd15a07f9306eea76005a8045b381b3cb66311b7b0d0e8b","reference":"cover-semantic-review-014.json","limitation":"Front title/author and source-edition binding; no barcode or exact printing-year claim."}],"review_status":"approved","reviewed_at":"2026-11-03T08:04:14.628Z","review_batch":"nl-scale-20261102-038"}},{"ref":"w7","relation":"works","key":{"native_identity_key":"nlscale:20261102:ol:OL719954W"},"before":null,"after":{"title":"Ik had een wapenbroeder","author_id":654,"first_publish_year":1973,"open_library_id":"OL719954W","cover_id":6452298,"source_type":"open_library","work_type":"novel","native_identity_key":"nlscale:20261102:ol:OL719954W"}},{"ref":"e7","relation":"editions","key":{"open_library_edition_id":"OL5495005M"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":"@w7","open_library_edition_id":"OL5495005M","isbn_13":"9789029518703","isbn_10":null,"title":"Ik had een wapenbroeder","language":"dut","publisher":"De Arbeiderspers"}},{"ref":"d7","relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","key":{"work_id":"@w7","language":"nl"},"before":null,"after":{"work_id":"@w7","language":"nl","bound_author_id":654,"text":"Een jonge dienstplichtige groeit op met de overtuigingen van zijn gereformeerde omgeving, maar ontdekt gevoelens die daar moeilijk in passen. In het leger raakt hij sterk verbonden met een mederekruut. Hun verhouding brengt vragen over verlangen, identiteit en loyaliteit naar voren, terwijl het militaire bestaan weinig ruimte laat voor persoonlijke kwetsbaarheid. Maarten ’t Hart onderzoekt hoe iemand zijn eigen ervaringen probeert te begrijpen tegenover de verwachtingen van anderen. De spanning binnen die verhouding werkt door in de gebeurtenissen tijdens hun diensttijd.","source_type":"official_catalog","source_name":"Gecontroleerde boek- en catalogusbronnen","source_url":"https://www.singeluitgeverijen.nl/de-arbeiderspers/boek/ik-had-een-wapenbroeder/","evidence":[{"type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p127249230","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p800282124","https://d